nts of $U$ that are not in $A$ are the integers $0$ through $39.$\n\nTherefore, the complement of $X$ is\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{X}={0,1,2,…,39}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295957 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "49251196-c06b-5718-82e6-5ed9450301af" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Complement of a Set Given Using Ellipsis Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "187cba77-f857-5469-b455-5f6a6691232d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{l,m,n…,z}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295959} {:answer/id #uuid "c26bc20f-a72b-5992-a3c6-8f4857574ac8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{m,n,o…,z}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295960} {:answer/id #uuid "4f224627-7277-5745-84a3-0aa30bd95e89" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{k,l,m,…,z}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295961} {:answer/id #uuid "c5a55504-c71b-58a3-a833-7bf431445e73" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{i,j,k,…,z}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295962} {:answer/id #uuid "672d52a6-0470-57f7-87f2-b17d8586b6df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{j,k,l…,z}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295963}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4f224627-7277-5745-84a3-0aa30bd95e89" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{k,l,m,…,z}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295961} :answer-field/id #uuid "bf5cbd0f-271d-5b9e-9396-5e93c5853b31" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295958}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "00d20e46-5a15-5da8-864f-78bbef842ab5" :question/math-academy-id "q-105188" :question/problem "Let $U={a,b,c,…,z}$ be the universal set and $Y={a,b,c,…,j}$, then $\\overset{―}{Y}=$" :question/worked-solution "The complement of $Y,$ denoted $\\overset{―}{Y},$ consists of every element in the universal set $U$ that is not in the set $Y.$\n\nThe universal set $U$ consists of the letters $a$ through $z,$ while the set $Y$ consists of the letters $a$ through $j.$\n\nSo, the only elements of $U$ that are not in $Y$ are the letters $k$ through $z.$\n\nTherefore, the complement of $Y$ is\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{Y}={k,l,m,…,z}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295964 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "49251196-c06b-5718-82e6-5ed9450301af" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Complement of a Set Given Using Ellipsis Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "98ae6423-be95-52fe-9825-782b07c36736" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{0,2,4,…}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295966} {:answer/id #uuid "01408247-3063-5f7f-ba03-ed3b2ed79628" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{0,1,2,…}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295967} {:answer/id #uuid "7ed54dd5-f073-5938-9117-b7f164b9e670" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{1,2,3,…}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295968} {:answer/id #uuid "9f38327a-25ba-585d-9132-8949cda042c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{1,3,5,…}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295969} {:answer/id #uuid "a8fe6e47-2425-590d-a37e-aa3ab173845a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The set of integers" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295970}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7ed54dd5-f073-5938-9117-b7f164b9e670" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{1,2,3,…}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295968} :answer-field/id #uuid "5fb782f7-8ff8-5158-a89d-20b131de75e7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295965}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "349803da-dde5-5e45-a05e-595d8b8224c2" :question/math-academy-id "q-105192" :question/problem "If the set $U$ containing all integers is the universal set and $X={0,-1,-2,-3,-4,…}$, then $\\overset{―}{X}=$" :question/worked-solution "The complement of $X,$ denoted $\\overset{―}{X},$ consists of every element in the universal set $U$ that is not in the set $X.$\n\nThe universal set $U$ consists of the integer numbers while the set $X$ consists of the negative integers and $0.$\n\nSo, the only elements of $U$ that are not in $X$ are the natural numbers.\n\nTherefore, the complement of $X$ is\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{X}={1,2,3,…}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295971 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "19fb3196-439e-5466-b50c-615c492167b4" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Complement of a Set Using a Venn Diagram"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "015bb249-de28-5690-bee6-711a5e6e2d9f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{♣,♡,△}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295973} {:answer/id #uuid "18b70ff8-e7b3-5941-8e78-efbba9019f14" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{△}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295974} {:answer/id #uuid "4327ed1e-838e-5f90-8514-c4dd2f20755d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{♡,△}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295975} {:answer/id #uuid "4984ba7f-fa6d-5f02-9e59-502f2eb8d4a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{♣,♡}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295976} {:answer/id #uuid "a06efe09-af7d-5de6-8f30-d5cb33426d22" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{♣,△}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295977}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "015bb249-de28-5690-bee6-711a5e6e2d9f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{♣,♡,△}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295973} :answer-field/id #uuid "b72f6a32-cfab-55b6-a75d-426a13c69140" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295972}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6909500f-